freetype: take the text and outline opacity while text shows

freetype-opacity and freetype-outline-opacity, like the colors before
patches/0004, are read once when the text renderer is created, so a player
that changes them while it plays never sees the change. Read them in
UpdateDefaultLiveStyles() with the colors; lines rendered after the change
take it.

Carried by Ferricone Player on top of VLC a5538c55; written for upstream.

diff --git i/modules/text_renderer/freetype/freetype.c w/modules/text_renderer/freetype/freetype.c
--- i/modules/text_renderer/freetype/freetype.c
+++ w/modules/text_renderer/freetype/freetype.c
@@ -716,7 +716,9 @@ static bool UpdateDefaultLiveStyles( filter_t *p_filter )
     bool b_new_family = false;
 
     p_style->i_font_color = var_InheritInteger( p_filter, "freetype-color" );
+    p_style->i_font_alpha = var_InheritInteger( p_filter, "freetype-opacity" );
     p_style->i_outline_color = var_InheritInteger( p_filter, "freetype-outline-color" );
+    p_style->i_outline_alpha = var_InheritInteger( p_filter, "freetype-outline-opacity" );
 
     p_style->i_background_alpha = var_InheritInteger( p_filter, "freetype-background-opacity" );
     p_style->i_background_color = var_InheritInteger( p_filter, "freetype-background-color" );
